"paths": {
"/v1/chat/completions": {
"post": {
"tags": [
"Chat"
],
"summary": "Create Chat Completion",
"description": "# Important Notes for Llama 4\n\n## 1. Streaming Finish Reason [Non-Standard]\n\nWhen streaming, the API currently returns `\"finish_reason\": \"None\"` in the final chunk rather than the standard `\"tool_calls\"`. This is a non-standard behavior and will be fixed in a future update.\n\n- **Handling:** Ensure your streaming logic treats `None` as a valid termination state for tool invocations.\n- **Future Updates:** This is a temporary behavior. The API will be updated in a future release to be fully compliant with the standard protocol.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Prompt-Based Tool Calling\n\nLlama 4 uses a specific prompt-based mechanism for function calling. Avoid adding conflicting tool instructions to your prompts, as this may prevent responses from being parsed correctly.\n\n- **Automatic Parsing:** The API automatically parses the syntax: `[func_name(params_name=params_value, ...)]`. You do not need to implement custom parsing for this format.\n- **Best Practice:** To ensure compatibility with Llama 4 and future models, do not include custom formatting rules in your system or user prompts. Adding custom instructions may require you to handle the parsing manually.\n- **No Mixed Content:** Llama 4 supports either a tool call or a text response, but not both in the same turn.\n    - Do not ask the model to \"explain its logic\" or provide a preamble before calling a tool.\n    - Support for mixed content (reasoning + tool calls) varies by model and may be available in future API updates.",
"operationId": "create_chat_completion_v1_chat_completions_post",
"requestBody": {
"content": {
"application/json": {
"schema": {
"$ref": "#/components/schemas/ChatCompletionRequest"
}
}
},
"required": true
},
"responses": {
"200": {
"description": "Successful Response",
"content": {
"application/json": {
"schema": {
"$ref": "#/components/schemas/ChatCompletionResponse"
}
}
}
},
"422": {
"description": "Validation Error",
"content": {
"application/json": {
"schema": {
"$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
}
}
}
}
}
}
},
